  "title": "Understanding Friedreich’s Ataxia",
  "summary": "Friedreich's ataxia typically begins between the ages of 5-15 with progressive difficulty walking and loss of coordination. The condition, caused by mutations in the FXN gene, affects approximately 1 in 40,000 people and is the most common inherited ataxia.",
